# Addon listing — tkmm.config

Every addon under `Addons/<Name>/` has a `tkmm.config`. TKMM and the site read the public name, one-liner, icon, description, features, and commands from this file. Do not invent those in TKMM or on the site, and do not put the one-liner, description, features, or commands in the TOC.

## File

```
publicName: Junk Master
oneLiner: Sells gray junk at vendors and keeps a ledger of what was sold.
icon: icon.png

---

Gray items with a vendor price sell when you open a vendor.

## Features

- The ledger lists each sale and what it was worth.

## Commands

- `/jm` opens the ledger.
```

- `publicName`, `oneLiner`, and `icon` are single lines. `icon` is a path relative to the addon folder, usually `icon.png`.
- `publicName` is the name players see. Spaces and punctuation are fine, including `?`. Leave it blank and the folder name is used. The folder name is the addon identity (`Addons/JunkMaster`, `JunkMaster.toc`) and cannot contain `\ / : * ? " < > |`.
- `## Title` in the TOC is that same public name, so the game's addon list matches. When `publicName` is blank, `## Title` is the folder name.
- `oneLiner` is one sentence. The detail page shows that sentence under the heading One Liner.
- A line that is only `---` ends the header. The prose after it, up to the first `##` heading, is the description.
- `## Features` lists what the player can do. `## Commands` lists the slash commands. Each item is a `- ` line. A bullet only counts when it sits under that heading.
- Do not list `tkmm.config` in the TOC. The client loads only the files the TOC names.

## TOC

The TOC keeps what the client needs to load and version the addon:

- `## Interface`
- `## Title`
- `## Version` (same value as `Main.lua`)
- `## SavedVariables` when the addon saves
- The load list

Notes, author, category, and icon texture do not belong in the TOC.
